### Key Research Resources Identified

**Papers:**
1. NeurIPS Noise Experiment (arXiv:2011.01469) - σ² ≈ 0.3-0.5
2. Strategyproof Peer Selection (arXiv:1806.06266) - Multiple equilibria
3. LLM Peer Review (arXiv:2310.01783) - AI capabilities
4. PeerReview4All (arXiv:1905.01989) - Capacity constraints
5. Shah et al. mechanism design papers
6. de Clippel et al. incentive mechanisms

**Datasets:**
- PeerRead (github.com/allenai/PeerRead)
- OpenReview API (openreview.net)
- Synthetic data with Beta(2,5) quality distribution

**Code:**
- PeerReview4All (github.com/niharshah/PeerReview4All)
- openreview-py (pip install openreview-py)

### Key Parameters for Simulation
- σ₀² = 0.3 (baseline noise from NeurIPS experiment)
- α = 0.5 (noise growth rate)
- τ = 0.25 (acceptance rate)
- Quality distribution: Beta(2,5)
